Mesa 26.2.6 for the Mali-G710 of the Google Pixel 7

The libraries are Mesa with the gallium drivers panfrost and softpipe, its EGL
with the platform "genode", and libdrm with a back end for the Gpu session of
the driver 'panthor_gpu' of the Genode tree, protocol
'include/gpu/panthor_session.h' of the api archive 'gpu_panthor'.

The EGL platform loads 'mesa26_gpu.lib.so', route this ROM to the back end:
'mesa26_gpu-panfrost.lib.so' or 'mesa26_gpu-softpipe.lib.so'.

Mesa generates part of its sources at build time, and the libpan shaders of
panfrost need LLVM, clang, and the SPIR-V translator. So the import runs a meson
build of Mesa on the host, 'files/generate.sh', which needs these tools, and takes
the files of 'files/generated.list' into 'src/generated'.

The file lists and the source lists in 'files/mk' were derived from a complete
meson build, they must be updated with a new version of Mesa.
